          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "τοῖς δούλοις αὐτοῦ τοῖς ἐσκανδαλισμένοις",
          "english_quote": "The context is pastoral intercession, not ownership. Following project guidance, we reserve 'slave' where bonded status is theologically active; here the honorific sense fits 'servants'.",
          "issue": "The simplified edition independently retains metadata that contradicts the current consistent 'servant' policy and excludes ownership nuance without support from this phrase. Pastoral intercession does not establish that δοῦλος is only honorific. Its main-text 'servants' needs no replacement.",
          "suggested_revision": "Keep 'servants' and correct the metadata to describe the consistent reader-facing policy. Preserve bonded-status, belonging, and allegiance nuances in the alternatives or audit explanation without claiming that this context excludes them.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "οὕτω δὲ ἤρχετο τὸ θηρίον ῥοίζῳ, ὥστε δύνασθαι αὐτὸ πόλιν λυμᾶναι.",
          "english_quote": "It was coming with such a rushing roar that it could ravage a city[l].",
          "issue": "Against the Greek independently, 'roar' narrows the rushing noise to an animal vocalization that the selected wording does not establish. This specificity is inherited from the standard edition but is not justified by simplification or by the reported Palatina rendering.",
          "suggested_revision": "Consider 'It was coming with such a rushing sound that it could ravage a city.' Subject this candidate to fresh review, preserving both the sound and the source's degree/result capacity to ravage a city. Correct the accompanying rationale and versional comparison accordingly.",
          "severity": "major"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Both editions cover all ten paragraphs and retain the names, repeated prohibitions, prayer clauses, measurements, genitive ambiguity, restrictive movement statements, and four color groups. Contextual 'repentance' and reader-facing 'servants' are appropriate. Revision is needed for the added specificity of 'roar', inaccurate servant-policy metadata, and undisclosed opening antecedent supplementation. The witness notes otherwise distinguish the supplied reports' corrections, restorations, conjectures, and mediated evidence without requiring replacement of the selected working readings. This is a bounded model review of the supplied text and reports, not authentication of unseen manuscripts or certification of exhaustive collation; proposed replacements remain subject to fresh review."
